  "articleBody": "Getting your website seen by AI systems like Google AI Overviews and ChatGPT isn't always straightforward. Many businesses, even with good traditional SEO, make a few common blunders that inadvertently shut them off from AI visibility. Understanding these pitfalls can save you a lot of headache and help you qualify for those coveted AI citations.\n\n- [ ] **Blocking AI Crawlers with robots.txt or `noindex`** — Why it matters: Often, businesses set up robots.txt rules or `noindex` tags that prevent certain AI bots (like OpenAI's OAI-SearchBot) from accessing their content, mistakenly thinking general search rules apply. This makes your content completely invisible to them.\n- [ ] **Assuming `llms.txt` or Special AI Schema is Required** — Why it matters: Google, for instance, has stated that no special `.llms.txt` file or unique AI schema is needed. Focusing on these non-existent requirements distracts from actual best practices.\n- [ ] **Structured Data Doesn't Match Visible Content** — Why it matters: Your JSON-LD schema needs to perfectly reflect the content on your page. If there are discrepancies, AI systems lose trust in your data and are less likely to use it.\n- [ ] **Relying on Text in Images or JavaScript Widgets** — Why it matters: AI crawlers struggle with extracting information embedded in images or hidden behind complex JavaScript. Keep your core answers and facts in clean, crawlable HTML text.\n- [ ] **Publishing Generic, AI-Generated Pages Without Review** — Why it matters: Creating a massive volume of unedited, AI-generated content without adding unique value, clear authorship, or fact-checking can lead to it being ignored. AI prioritizes fact density and relevance.\n- [ ] **Ignoring Server Logs and Crawler Test Data** — Why it matters: These logs are goldmines for understanding how crawlers interact with your site. Without reviewing them, you might miss critical errors or access issues only visible from the server side.\n\n**How to use this checklist**\nGo through your website or have a professional review these items specifically. This isn't just about general SEO; it's about making sure your site's technical foundations and content structure are explicitly optimized for AI consumption. Many of these issues are technical and require specific knowledge to diagnose and fix effectively, ensuring AI systems can confidently find and cite your business.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-23"
